   "stem": {
      "text": "Let f be a function with a continuous derivative for all real x, where \\( f(2) = -1 \\), \\( f'(2) = 1 \\) and \\( f(6) = -6 \\), \\( f'(6) = 6 \\). Find \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{f(3x) + 6}{x^{2} - 4} \\), showing the work that justifies the method.",
