   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Check the form first: \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\left(f(3x) + 6\\right) = f(6) + 6 = -6 + 6 = 0 \\) and \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\left(x^{2} - 4\\right) = 0 \\), so the limit has the form 0/0.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "verify the indeterminate form"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By L'Hospital's rule, differentiate the numerator and the denominator separately, using the chain rule on \\( f(3x) \\): \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{3 f'(3x)}{2 x} = \\frac{3(6)}{4} = \\frac{9}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
